{title: You Are Good}
{artist: Bethel Music}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
Electric guitar (2 rounds)
[A] [E/G#] [A] [C#m] [D] [E]
[A] [E/G#] [A] [C#m] [D]
[A]

{comment: Verse 1}
[A]I want to scream it out, from every mountain [D]top
Your goodness knows no bounds, Your goodness never [F#m]stops
Your mercy follows me, Your kindness [E/G#]fills my [A]life
Your Love amazes me

{comment: Chorus 1}
I [A]sing because You are good, and I dance because You are good
And I [D]shout because You are good, You are good, good to me

{comment: Intro}
[A] [E/G#] - [A] - [C#m] - [D] [E] [A] [E/G#] - [A] - [C#m] - [D] (hang)

{comment: Verse 2}
[A]Nothing and no one comes, anywhere [F#m]clos[E]e [F#m]to Y[D]ou
The earth and oceans deep, only re[C#m]flect [E]this [F#m]truth
And in my darkest night, You shine as [E/G#]bright as [A]day
Your love amazes [E]me

{comment: Chorus 2}
I [A]sing because You are good, and I dance because Y[E/G#]ou ar[A]e [C#m]good
And I [D]shout because You are good, You are good, good to me [E]

{comment: Bridge}
With a [Bm7]cry of praise my heart [D]will proclaim, You are [A]good, You are good
In the [Bm7]sun or rain my life [D]celebrates, You are [A]good, You are good
